\" class=\"sf-depth-1 sf-no-children sf-last\" role=\"none\"><a href=\"/delivering-results\" class=\"sf-depth-1\" role=\"menuitem\">Delivering Results</a></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"evo-navbar-right\"><div class=\"views-exposed-form block block--ruiz-evo-custom-61-solr-search-2\" role=\"search\" data-drupal-selector=\"views-exposed-form-evo-search-api-solr-index-page-1-edit-views-exposed-form\"><form block=\"ruiz_evo_custom_61_solr_search_2\" action=\"/search\" method=\"get\" id=\"views-exposed-form-evo-search-api-solr-index-page-1-edit-views-exposed-form\" accept-charset=\"UTF-8\"><div class=\"js-form-item form-item js-form-type-textfield form-item-search-api-fulltext js-form-item-search-api-fulltext form-no-label form-group\"><input placeholder=\"Enter keywords\" aria-label=\"Enter keywords to search content.\" data-drupal-selector=\"edit-search-api-fulltext\" type=\"text\" id=\"edit-search-api-fulltext\" name=\"search_api_fulltext\" value=\"\" size=\"30\" maxlength=\"128\" class=\"form-control\" /></div><div data-drupal-selector=\"edit-actions-edit-views-exposed-form\" class=\"form-actions js-form-wrapper form-wrapper\" id=\"edit-actions-edit-views-exposed-form\"><input data-drupal-selector=\"edit-submit-evo-search-api-solr-index\" type=\"submit\" id=\"edit-submit-evo-search-api-solr-index\" value=\"Search\" class=\"button js-form-submit form-submit btn btn-primary\" /></div></form></div></div></div></div></nav><!-- NAVBAR END --></div><main class=\"evo-main\"><!--  USERBAR --><section class=\"page__userbar evo-userbar\"><div class=\"container d-flex\"><div class=\"flex-fill mr-auto evo-userbar-first\"><div data-drupal-messages-fallback class=\"hidden\"></div></div></div></section><!--  USERBAR END --><!--  PREFACE --><!--  PREFACE END --><!-- POPUP --><!-- POPUP END --><!-- CONTENT --><div class=\"page__content evo-page-content\"><div class=\"container\"><section class=\"page__breadcrumb evo-breadcrumb\"><div class=\"block block--ruiz-evo-custom-61-breadcrumbs\"><nav aria-label=\"breadcrumb\" class=\"\"><ol class=\"breadcrumb\"><li class=\"breadcrumb-item \"><a href=\"/\">Home</a></li><li class=\"breadcrumb-item \"><a href=\"/media-center\">Media</a></li><li class=\"breadcrumb-item \"><a href=\"/media-center/in-the-news\">In the News</a></li></ol></nav></div></section><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col evo-content\"><a id=\"main-content\"></a><div class=\"block block--ruiz-evo-custom-61-page-title\"><h1 class=\"display-4\"><span>Coachella&#039;s &#039;godfather of boxing,&#039; Lee Espinoza, honored in Congress</span></h1></div><div class=\"block block--ruiz-evo-custom-61-content\"><article class=\"node evo-in-the-news evo-in-the-news--full\"><div><div  class=\"row evo-create-type\"><div class=\"col-auto\">July 29, 2022 </div><div class=\"col-auto\"><a href=\"/media-center/in-the-news\" alt=\"View In The News listings\">In The News</a></div></div><div class=\"evo-in-the-news__field-evo-byline\"><p>Eliana Perez</p></div><div class=\"evo-in-the-news__field-evo-source-url\"><a href=\"https://www.desertsun.com/story/news/local/coachella/2022/07/29/coachellas-boxing-lee-espinoza-honored-congress/10179583002/\">Palm Springs Desert Sun</a></div><div class=\"evo-in-the-news__body\"><p><div class=\"media-item media-image full\"><div class=\"image__field-media-image\"><div class=\"field__label font-weight-bold visually-hidden\">\n      Image    </div><div class=\"field__item\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/evo-subsites/ruiz-evo.house.gov/files/wysiwyg_uploaded/635728663751568749-Boxing-Desert-Showdown15324.jpg\" width=\"660\" height=\"373\" alt=\"espinoza\" class=\"img-fluid\"></div></div></div></p><p>Librado \"Lee\" Espinoza, the famed coach and owner of a Coachella boxing club, was honored in Congress this week for his impact on the community and beyond as well as the lasting mark he's left on the sport.</p><p>Espinoza, 74, is a world-renowned coach who has trained numerous champions in the past 40 years. He was inducted into the California Boxing Hall of Fame in 2005 and the West Coast Boxing Hall of Fame in 2021.</p><p>As Rep. Raul Ruiz paid tribute, he spoke about the influence Espinoza's had on him and what he means to the valley as a whole.</p><p>\"Growing up in Coachella, I know that I was personally inspired by Lee and his grit, determination, and work ethic,\" said Ruiz, a Democrat who represents the valley. \"I looked up to Lee because I knew he was making a difference in our humble farmworker community. And it is my hope that by telling his story here today and recording it in our nation's history, athletes across the country and future generations will also be inspired and will feel that same sense of hope that he has given to our valley.\"</p><p>On Thursday, The Desert Sun caught up with Espinoza to talk about receiving this honor. \"There's no words for me to describe this. My tears came down when somebody told me, 'Your name is now in Washington, D.C.' It's just really, really incredible,\" he said.</p><p><div class=\"media-item media-image full\"><div class=\"image__field-media-image\"><div class=\"field__label font-weight-bold visually-hidden\">\n      Image    </div><div class=\"field__item\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/evo-subsites/ruiz-evo.house.gov/files/wysiwyg_uploaded/13c4e91e-9510-423b-bc89-c11ac31d2184-Ruiz_on_Lee_Espinoza.jpg\" width=\"660\" height=\"372\" alt=\"house floor\" class=\"img-fluid\"></div></div></div></p><p>Espinoza and his mother moved to the United States from Mexico when he was much younger, following the death of his father. After he started a family of his own, one of Espinoza's sons, Ruben, took a special interest in boxing, leading Espinoza to pick up coaching.</p><p>Espinoza eventually opened the Coachella Valley Boxing Club next to Coachella City Hall in 1985 and, in 1996, moved it to the spot near Bagdouma Park where it remains today. Espinoza said he credits the club, or \"the school,\" as he also calls it, for the successes of himself and his \"students.\"</p><p>\"You see a little town like Coachella and yet, all these kids from here, they go on to win all over the world<strong>,\"</strong> Espinoza said.<strong> \"</strong>Some coaches, you know, some of them get lucky, where they get boxers that are already (trained). But here, I've (trained) them since they were little.\"</p><p>Among those he's trained are the Diaz brothers, Joel, Jesus, Antonio and Julio, each of whom has won national titles and competed before international audiences; Randy Caballero, an International Boxing Federation World Champion; and Jocelyn Camarillo, the 2021 winner of the USA Boxing National Championships.</p><p>Espinoza emphasized that any boxing community in the world knows great boxers are made in Coachella and that he's had a hand in their illustrious careers. </p><p>Ruiz recognized that at the House, saying, \"Lee is truly the godfather of boxing in the valley. He has trained world champions and put Coachella on the map for producing some of the best boxers in the game.\"</p><p>Though Espinoza considers himself \"semi-retired\" — he said his age and an arm injury prevent him from getting in the ring — he is still a regular at the Coachella Valley Boxing Club where he instructs both boxers and other coaches on the sport.</p><p>He can also now indulge in simply being part of the audience, which he planned to do on Thursday night during the Fantasy Springs Resort Casino <a href=\"https://www.desertsun.com/story/sports/boxing/2022/07/26/coachella-boxer-manny-flores-looking-steal-show-again-dazn/10158200002/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">fights featuring Coachella's Manny Flores versus Daniel Colula</a> and Lucia Hernandez versus Gabriela Fundora, another Coachella native trained by Espinoza.</p><p>\"I just go enjoy it now. Yeah, I'm enjoying it,\" Espinoza said. </p></div><div class=\"evo-in-the-news__field-evo-issues d-flex\"><span class=\"field__label font-weight-bold\">\n      Issues<span class=\"field__label__suffix mr-2\">:</span></span><span class=\"field__items\"><span class=\"field__item mr-2\"><a href=\"/issues/senior-citizens\" hreflang=\"en\">Senior Citizens</a></span></span></div></div></article></div></div></div></div></div><!-- CONTENT END --><!-- POSTSCRIPT --><section class=\"container evo-postscript d-flex\"><div class=\"evo-postscript-first flex-fill mr-auto\"><div class=\"views-element-container block block--ruiz-evo-custom-61-evo-office-locations-block-map\"><div block=\"ruiz_evo_custom_61_evo_office_locations_block_map\"><div class=\"office-locations js-view-dom-id-7098472b19ff9d7be54a55903b39d7a0edbb96122400c5cbf9653b074663a5ab\"><div class=\"evo-view-evo-office-locations evo-view-wrapper\"><div class=\"evo-views-row-container\"><div class=\"views-row evo-views-row views-row-0 views-row-first\"><div class=\"views-field views-field-nothing\"><div class=\"field-content\"><section aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"evo-map-office-coordinates-wrapper\"><span class=\"evo-map-lat\">38.8868782</span><span class=\"evo-map-long\">-77.0102282</span></section></div></div></div><div class=\"views-row evo-views-row views-row-1\"><div class=\"views-field views-field-nothing\"><div class=\"field-content\"><section aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"evo-map-office-coordinates-wrapper\"><span class=\"evo-map-lat\">33.768462740983</span><span class=\"evo-map-long\">-116.30506225942</span></section></div></div></div><div class=\"views-row evo-views-row views-row-2\"><div class=\"views-field views-field-nothing\"><div class=\"field-content\"><section aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"evo-map-office-coordinates-wrapper\"><span class=\"evo-map-lat\">33.74755457272285</span><span class=\"evo-map-long\">-116.96788948893054</span></section></div></div></div><div class=\"views-row evo-views-row views-row-3 views-row-last\"><div class=\"views-field views-field-nothing\"><div class=\"field-content\"><section aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"evo-map-office-coordinates-wrapper\"><span